NOTE ON SCOPE

This MIT licence covers the CODE in this repository: everything under tools/
and any code inside reproductions/ and tutorials/.

The WRITTEN material - the paper summaries, and anything else here that is
prose rather than code - is licensed CC BY 4.0 instead. See COPYRIGHT.md for
the authoritative path-to-licence map, and LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt for that
licence.

MIT is kept at this canonical path so GitHub's licence detector, the repository
badge and the API all read cleanly. The split exists because a software licence
says nothing sensible about a paper summary: MIT grants the right to use,
modify and sublicense a work "as software", which is not the permission a
reader of prose needs, and it asks for a copyright notice rather than
attribution to an author.
